# Gate review, round 2 — M-next D13, the driver's candidate half

Read-only; nothing edited, no suite run (per the task constraints — so the current 27-deftest file's green is verified by reading, not by execution; the collab findings file documents green only for the round-1 12-test version). Reviewed: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc` (1045 lines), `test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver_test.cljc` (1367 lines), the D plan r3, the D10 lower-inputs ruling, and the landed seams the driver composes (`dao/lease.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/ledger.cljc`, `holder/evidence.cljc`, `holder/writer.cljc`, `holder/reader.cljc`, `authority/front.cljc`, `authority/grant.cljc`, `handoff.cljc`).

## Verdict: NOT READY

All ten opus findings and all four astra sign-off items are verified fixed in the code, and almost every one is pinned by a test. One regression-shaped defect introduced by the astra-1 fix must change before landing, plus two cheap test pins:

1. **A run ended inside the post-cycle drain is not short-circuited** (`driver.cljc:939-957`) — must add the `:releasing` guard the pre-cycle drain already has (`driver.cljc:904`). Detail in finding 1 below.
2. **Pin the judge-rejection → fresh-proposal half** of the proposal discipline (code `driver.cljc:478-481`, `483`); only the carriage-failure half is pinned (finding 2).
3. **(Recommended, not blocking) Pin the epoch dimension** of the running-phase tenure recheck (`driver.cljc:924-926`); only the lease dimension is pinned (finding 3).

Everything else below is verified and can land as-is once item 1 is fixed and item 2 is pinned.

## A. The opus round-1 findings — verification

**F1 — grants must answer a proposal this driver sent. VERIFIED.** `accept` constructs the dao.lease holder with both expectations — `:subject (custody/subject (:occurrence state))` and `:proposal (:dao.lease/proposal fact)` (`driver.cljc:558-565`) — and `lease/observe-grant` enforces them: the fact must name `:self` as holder, the grantor by the resolver, and match both expectations (`dao/lease.cljc:1774-1785`). Outstanding ids are tracked: `:sent-proposals` is a set conj'd only when the append answered `:dao.stream/ok` (`driver.cljc:496-499`), and the raw grant scan filters on it (`driver.cljc:694`) — a grant carrying no pid, or a pid this driver never sent, never reaches `accept`. Tests: activating grants either come from the judge (`two-candidates-over-two-encodings-test`, `driver_test.cljc:504-540`) or answer the driver's own live pid via the authority's own ledger writer (`own-grant-driver`, `driver_test.cljc:493-497`; `the-source-resumes-only-after-its-own-grant-test` at `:970`); foreign pids appear only where non-activation is the point (`foreign-grants-never-activate-a-restarted-driver-test`, `:1049-1057`; the "p-x" grant to holder-b at `:963`).

**F2 — the D7 pipeline before checkpoint/inspect in :validating. VERIFIED.** `step-validating` runs `handoff/resume-task` with no `:grant` first and calls `checkpoint/inspect` only after an `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` answer (`driver.cljc:995-1013`). `resume-task*` runs the D7 order — two-codec decode, tag, version gate, then its own version-1 inspect — and refuses `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` in `accept-grant!` before `attach-all!` (`handoff.cljc:1818-1843`, `:1698-1699`), so nothing is attached and no machine is exposed. The 7.2.1 order is pinned by `profile-refusal-precedes-wrong-address-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1060-1069`): version-2 bytes under v1's address answer `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, not `:yin.k/hash-mismatch`, with zero attaches and no request — the version gate (`handoff.cljc:1645-1665`) provably precedes the address check. Zero side effects in :validating additionally pinned at `:986-1002` (junk bytes, no attach, no request).

**F3 — the stale-grant branch mints once. VERIFIED.** `accept`'s stale-branch resets `:proposal` to nil only when `(:dao.lease/proposal fact)` equals the current outstanding id (`driver.cljc:594-596`), and `propose` mints only when `:proposal` is nil or the projection's `:answered` says `:dao.lease/rejected` (`driver.cljc:477-487`). On later steps the stale fact's pid no longer matches, so the outstanding successor is resent, not re-minted. Pinned by `stale-own-grant-mints-only-one-successor-proposal-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1072-1083`): after the lapse, five drives produce exactly 2 proposals and 2 distinct pids (a real lapse through the writer, `lapse-direct!` at `:400-402`, which commits lapse+reclaimed as one foldable transaction per `grant.cljc:256-279`).

**F4 — the admit-routing test. VERIFIED.** `enrolled-write-after-activation-routes-both-answer-paths-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1296-1333`) drives a real enrolled first-export write (an enrolled retained write with a predecessor op id cannot reach D13 activation — the boundary is documented at `:914-921` — so the test enrolls the target at the source, `header-of 0 #{target} false` at `:1314`) through both answer paths: by reply (`read-outcome!` disabled, `:1326`) and by projected outcome (an admit-skipping reply reader, `:1320-1325`). `drain` routes `:yin.k/admit`-kind records to `writer/discharge` and wrapper-less `:yin.k/admission` records to `writer/discharge`'s projected arm (`driver.cljc:774-779`; `writer.cljc:485-514`). Both paths reach `:safepoint`, `:done`, with the effect on the authority's target reader and an `:yin.k/admit` request asserted.

**F5 — the residual-2 regrant rows through the judge. VERIFIED.** `invalid-bindings-answer-not-holder-and-release-test`'s last block (`driver_test.cljc:690-710`): after holder-a's release, `judge! {:s 4}` and holder-b driven with `:judge {:s 5}` — a real proposal the judge grants, asserted at the authority's projection. `post-grant-failure-releases-or-retains-test`'s third block (`:792-799`) is stronger: holder-b activates to `:running` through the judge's own regrant. The residual-2 wording holds: `releasing`'s docstring and code release without clearing quarantine or completing anything (`driver.cljc:416-438`), and no test has the ended driver propose on behalf of recovery — only fresh candidates propose.

**F6 — the run ends at the lease bound even when the ledger is unreadable. VERIFIED.** `step-active-held` checks `lease/holding?` at `driver.cljc:900` before `read-ledger!` at `:903`; the nil-records branch answers `:unsatisfied` only when still holding (`:908-910`). Pinned by `unreadable-ledger-still-ends-at-local-bound-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1209-1217`): `read-ledger!` `(constantly nil)` at the bound answers `:releasing`/`:lease-bound` with the machine gated `:ended`.

**F7 — the tenure recheck covers the epoch. VERIFIED in code; pin is lease-only.** The running-phase stale check is `(or (not= l (:dao.lease/lease entry)) (not= (get-in state [:evidence :yin.k/binding :yin.k/epoch]) (:yin.k/epoch entry)))` (`driver.cljc:924-926`), and `accept`'s own `stale?` includes the epoch (`:556-557`); `:evidence`'s `:yin.k/binding` is `custody/binding-evidence`'s answer carrying `:yin.k/epoch` (`evidence.cljc:121-124`, `custody.cljc:202-206`), and the entry epoch is the fold's occurrence epoch (`ledger.cljc:68-73`). See finding 3 for the coverage gap.

**F8 — a real fold-defect test. VERIFIED.** `dense-ledger-with-invalid-content-is-a-fold-defect-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1129-1143`): the history stays dense (the record's `:t` untouched) while its datoms become an unpublished attribute — `history-defect` passes, the fold defects (`ledger.cljc:250-253` `:malformed-fact`), and the answer is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` `:fold-defect` with no machine, zero attaches, no release. This is genuinely distinct from the four unavailable modes (`driver_test.cljc:746-750`), which break density or shape first.

**F9 — the step state is plain data. VERIFIED.** `initial` returns one persistent map (`driver.cljc:176-200`); no atom, volatile, ref, promise or delay anywhere in the namespace (grep-verified; the only "atom" hits are the word "datoms"). The dao.lease holder is a plain map (`dao/lease.cljc:1623-1635`); the machine is the published task value. The one transient non-data construct — `guarded-handle` reify wrappers installed by `guard-writes` (`driver.cljc:801-833`) — is removed by `restore-handles` before the state is answered (`:836-843`, applied at `:867`), and on a mid-cycle throw `step-active`'s catch ends the run from the pre-cycle state (`:961-969`), so wrappers never persist in the state. `:seams` holds the composition-supplied functions by contract, not driver state.

**F10 — D3's evidence fold reused, not duplicated. VERIFIED, with a note.** The binding comes from `custody/binding-evidence` (`driver.cljc:549`) and the evidence `E` from `evidence/read-evidence` (`:552`) — D3's reader, not a reimplementation. The driver's private `history-defect` and `fold` (`driver.cljc:282-314`) mirror D3's private `defect`/`fold` (`evidence.cljc:47-72`) because the driver additionally needs the projection itself (occurrence state, admitted variants, `:answered`) and classified defect reasons, which `read-evidence` does not expose; both delegate to the shared public core `ledger/empty-projection`/`ledger/fold-record`. See finding 5 for the sync-risk note.

## B. The astra sign-off items — verification

**1 — renewal advances tenure only on authenticated matching :carried evidence; bound rechecked before delayed evidence. VERIFIED.** The renewal arm of `control-reply` requires `front/reply-evidence` (`driver.cljc:636-637`), the outstanding request id (`:660`), and `:yin.k/answer` `:carried` (`:661`); only then does it recheck `lease/holding?` with a fresh clock reading (`:662`) — past the bound it refuses the evidence and ends the run (`:669`) instead of advancing — and `observe-renewal` is fed the retained pre-send reading (`:664-668`), which `dao.lease` records only for an ok outcome and never at/past the bound (`dao/lease.cljc:1834-1856`). Nothing advances on inbound acceptance: `renew` discards the append outcome (`driver.cljc:756`). Pinned by `renewal-does-not-advance-on-queue-acceptance-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1102-1117`, both the no-advance and the late-evidence halves), `renewal-before-half-and-io-stops-at-the-bound-test` (`:806-872`, `last-renewal-at {:s 11}` = the pre-send reading, before half of 30), and `failed-renewal-carriage-retains-original-reading-test` (`:1146-1162`).

**2 — control-reply checks :yin.k/answer; release not completed on inbound acceptance; unchanged retries; rejection distinguished from carriage failure. VERIFIED, one pin missing (finding 2).** All three arms read `[:yin.k/answer :yin.k/status]` (`driver.cljc:647`, `654-655`, `661`). `step-releasing` moves to `:failed` only on `:carried` via `drain-control` (`:976-983`); an ok append only sets `:sent` (`:985-986`) — pinned by `release-does-not-finish-on-queue-acceptance-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1189-1206`). Retries unchanged: proposals (`queued-control-requests-need-authenticated-carriage-test`, `:1086-1099` — 2 sends, 1 distinct pid), renewals (`failed-renewal-carriage…`, 1 distinct request id), releases (`lost-control-replies-retry-unchanged-obligations-test`, `:1165-1186` — 2 sends, 1 distinct request-id, then `:failed` with `:carried`). Rejection vs carriage: `propose` mints fresh only on `:answered … :dao.lease/rejected` (`driver.cljc:478-481`); carriage failure resends the same pid; the judge's hook does reject losing proposals (`grant.cljc:289-329`), but no test drives that rejection through to the fresh mint — finding 2.

**3 — tenure rechecked before program IO including bare writes and closes. VERIFIED.** `run-cycle` tenure-gates every path: the cycle entry (`driver.cljc:853`), after computation+replay before emit (`:861`), the request appender and diagnostic fn passed to `writer/emit` (`:862-866`), the live-observation callback (`:868-871`), and — for the bare class, which `writer/emit` performs directly on the machine's own handle (`writer.cljc:373-380`, closes at `:328-337`) — `guard-writes` wraps every descriptor-satisfying handle in the tree with `guarded-handle`, whose `append!` and `close!` both call `require-tenure!` first (`driver.cljc:801-833`). Pinned by `tenure-is-rechecked-between-bare-effects-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1241-1269`: first append lands, resets the clock to the bound; the close and second put never run — `[1]` emitted, root and install child gated `:ended`, release retained) and `computation-cannot-spend-tenure-and-then-perform-io-test` (`:1272-1293`: a primitive spends the tenure mid-`vm/run`, zero effects performed).

**4 — thrown post-grant failures end the run with a retained release, no effect retry. VERIFIED.** The writer's terminal bare-link throw is reachable: `apply-effect` throws on a terminal link-request outcome (`writer.cljc:277-280`), reached through `emit`'s `:at-least-once` arm. `step-active` catches any throw, routes `::cause :lease-bound` to the bound end and everything else to `:program-failure` with the failure in the detail, both via `end-run` → `releasing` (`driver.cljc:961-969`, `:441-452`) — machine gated `:ended`, holder stopped, release sent at once and retained verbatim on a failed append (`:416-438`). Pinned by `terminal-bare-link-failure-retains-release-and-is-not-retried-test` (`driver_test.cljc:1336-1367`): one call to the failed effect, `:releasing`, `:ended`, `:failure` in detail, and the continued step retries only the release with the effect untouched.

## C. Findings

1. **[Must fix] A run ended inside the post-cycle drain is re-labeled by the step's cond.** `driver.cljc:939-957`. The pre-cycle drain's run-end is short-circuited (`(if (= :releasing (:phase state)) state …)`, `:904`), but the post-cycle drain's is not: `control-reply`'s renewal arm can call `end-run` inside `drain` (`:669`) — exactly the astra-1-mandated bound recheck before accepting delayed evidence — and the returned state then flows into the cond at `:943-957`, where `(some? unsat)` overwrites the `:yin.k/ended` status with `:yin.k/unsatisfied` (`phase` stays `:releasing`, the ended answer is lost), or `at-safepoint?` — true on a machine that halted this cycle and was gated `:ended` — flips `:phase` to `:safepoint` with `:status :yin.k/ok` (`:951-954`). The next step then re-ends the run: a **second** run-end diagnostic (violating r3 1.6 "one diagnostic") and a re-sent release (deduped by request id, but the composition saw a wrong `:ok` answer for a step whose run had ended). Reachability needs a reply that arrives while the driver steps (a `read-reply!` over a live remote stream — permitted, "no transport is known here") plus the clock crossing the bound during the cycle; it cannot fire under the test world's between-step atom clocks, which is why no test catches it. Fix: mirror `:904` — test `(:phase base)` for `:releasing` (or fold the drain's run-end into `:run-end`) before the cond.

2. **[Must pin] The judge-rejection → fresh-proposal half of the discipline is unpinned.** `propose`'s `refused?` (`driver.cljc:478-481`) is the astra-2 "rejection distinguished from carriage failure" rejection half; the carriage half is pinned (`driver_test.cljc:1086-1099`), the rejection half is not. `two-candidates-over-two-encodings-test` manufactures exactly this rejection (the judge's hook refuses holder-b in the same pass that grants holder-a, `grant.cljc:314-319`) but stops at `:not-holder` while the occurrence is held. A short extension — lapse/release lease-1, then step holder-b again and assert a fresh pid is proposed (the answered pid never reused, 7.7.8) — closes it.

3. **[Recommended] The epoch dimension of the running-phase recheck is unpinned.** `driver.cljc:924-926` rechecks lease and epoch; every stale/regrant test fires the lease dimension (a reclaim clears `:dao.lease/lease`, `ledger.cljc:622-625`). An epoch change with the lease id unchanged has no path through a foldable history (a reclaim requires its lapse in the same transaction, `ledger.cljc:753-761`), so the check is defense-in-depth — but since F7 was specifically about the epoch, one crafted-record test pinning it (and `accept`'s `:556-557`) would make the fix regression-proof.

4. **[Verified fixed, worth knowing] Two tenure readings per accepting step — resolved.** The round-1 concern is gone: one `reading` (`driver.cljc:566`) feeds both `observe-grant` and the lower's `:now` (`:615`), with `bound` computed from the grant's own basis and duration (`:509-536`).

5. **[Note] Residual duplication of D3's whole-history rule.** `driver.cljc:282-314` (`history-defect`, `fold`) restate `evidence.cljc:47-72` (`defect`, `fold`) with a different return convention. Today their semantics agree (both classify transport/start-past-origin/gap/fold-defect identically; the driver's `fold` also catches gaps via `ledger/fold-record`'s `:t-mismatch`, `ledger.cljc:726-727`). Two private copies of one normative rule is a sync hazard for future D-slices; exposing the whole-history check/fold from `evidence` (or `ledger`) and reusing it would remove it. Not blocking.

6. **[Note] `step-proposing`'s defect branches skip `drain-control`.** The `unsatisfied` branches at `driver.cljc:698-702` return without draining replies, unlike every other branch (`:697`, `:709`, `:715`, `:720`). Harmless (the next readable history drains; control state is only re-read, never lost), but asymmetric.

7. **[Note] Unverified green.** Per the read-only constraint I ran nothing. The collab findings file records round-1 green (12 tests/153 assertions JVM); the current file has 27 deftests and no recorded run in collab. The three-lane run and kondo/cljstyle remain the slice gate's duty as before.

## Regression sweep (nothing else found)

Checked and clean: the `:sent-proposals` filter cannot be seeded by never-sent pids (`driver.cljc:496-499`); resends are idempotent for pid tracking; the stale-branch reset cannot loop (answered `:accepted` pids never satisfy `refused?`); `step-releasing`'s resend-until-carried (including after `:sent`) matches the idempotent release carriage contract (`front.cljc:92-95`, judge answers once); the `drain` routing sends each record to exactly one arm and re-passes it through `control-reply`, whose arms require their own reply kinds (`driver.cljc:774-791`, `640-671`); discharge/settle are idempotent against a second copy of the same answer (entry gone → `:no_entry`/`:no-held` retained); the double `checkpoint/inspect` (once inside the D7 pipeline, once at `:1007` for the baseline) is pure and cannot reorder refusals; `guard-writes`/`restore-handles` are path-symmetric over the machine tree and their wrappers cannot survive into the state, including on throw; `:safepoint` still renews and rechecks (`driver.cljc:1043` case group; safepoint reached and asserted in `driver_test.cljc:879-909`); the halted-result safepoint with no lease steps to itself (`driver.cljc:898-899`); the invalid-binding cond order in `accept` correctly answers before the (defecting) projection is consulted, and a broken fold cannot hide the driver's own grant because the raw scan precedes it (`driver.cljc:329-343`, `694-697`); `:malformed-record` correctly falls to `unsatisfied` rather than the release-owing invalid set (`driver.cljc:397-402` vs `custody.cljc:171-174`).
